# Omarchy migrations that must never run here. The user unit marks each one
# complete for every account, so omarchy-migrate stops offering it.
#
# Every migration runs unless it cannot run without a risk of bricking this
# ZFS host (ADR 0005). Each row says which risk.

# Installs linux-omarchy and its headers, then rebuilds and checks its Limine
# entry with limine-entry-tool, which this host deliberately lacks, so it can
# never complete here. The kernel itself is wanted (ADR 0008): PACMAN_PACKAGES
# installs it with zfs-dkms, beside the linux-cachyos fallback.
1789325478.sh

# Moves [omarchy] above every other repository and runs a full upgrade.
# [omarchy] carries quickshell, nvidia dkms builds, kernels and the real
# limine packages, which would then win over CachyOS and the boot stub.
1791403252.sh

# Replaces CachyOS's power-profiles-daemon with [omarchy]'s build through
# pacman -S. It is meant for ARM laptops but checks only that the stock
# package is installed, so it fires on x86 too. The build is the same 0.30
# with NVIDIA Spark and Snapdragon profiles; on these boxes it gains nothing
# and moves the power daemon from CachyOS to [omarchy].
1791554699.sh

# Renames the hibernation resume device and runs omarchy-hibernation-setup,
# which bin.deny blocks. It acts only on a Limine resume drop-in and the
# omarchy_resume mkinitcpio hook, and this host has neither.
1792965062.sh
